  "problem": "Core research tasks lacked documented keyboard and assistive-technology limits. Automated scanners could be treated as WCAG certification. Untested screen-reader combinations could be marked passed. The 360px menu button shrank below 44px.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Automated checks identify issues but do not alone certify accessibility; their actual findings are preserved. Keyboard source checks cover search, menus, filters, dictionary, shortlist, comparison and export without claiming a mouse-free browser session that was not run. Target sizes and contrast tokens are measured. Assistive-technology combinations that were not run remain untested, not passed. No WCAG 2.2 AA conformance claim is inferred from a scanner or screenshot. Six result-card regions remain. The mobile menu closes on Escape and stays 44px at 360px. plan_research remains disabled. worker/index.mjs does not import enrichment. HTTP 200 is not a completed research task. Last-good generation live-2026-09-03-85b50522b420 is unchanged.",
